                <pb facs="0768" n="674" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg674"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">817.51/2171: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hanna</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Managua</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-08-09T15:00:00-05:45">August 9, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 4:39 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>100. Department’s 80, August 8, 5 p.m. I appreciate the Department’s support in
                    the matter of the Guardia agreement. I hear [<hi rendition="#italic">hope?</hi>]
                    you may also induce the Nicaraguan Legation to cooperate in this matter. My
                    negotiations would be hindered if that Legation should transmit the Department’s
                    reply to Dr. Carazo in a form which would irritate President Moncada.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hanna</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
